ayloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8261293343635520aa6bf86fb8286c02c5b4e0d69f5f2e87de70c80defe2d660","event_uuid":"79a54098-275a-47e9-81c3-0da9e5c43736","position":{"commit_sha":"203be1beb12ab43b49c6b0f48c5fd0fb84f748c5","position":"1785252433199808001-79a54098-275a-47e9-81c3-0da9e5c43736"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cb39e3216fb703eba0ea8f89fbd90357eba345d20133da0b9bae1d208aa99c65","event_uuid":"bae0d851-715e-4111-a598-a5c06851ec17","position":{"commit_sha":"0da5bd7806bb262324d0da3fcd9e9c2fc70e7868","position":"1785252450957128001-bae0d851-715e-4111-a598-a5c06851ec17"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 complete; Phase 2 test contract frozen. Runtime reproduction through public adapter.code_review_decision with 11 blocking findings, each >240 chars, produced a header claiming 11 issues, exactly 10 bullets, and bullets clipped mid-token with no ellipsis/overflow disclosure. Proven changeable cause: src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py:120 iterates blocking[:10] and line 122 slices normalized detail[:240], while lines 123-125 append/return without either disclosure branch. Alternative that another layer discloses omission is rejected: voter.py posts decision[\"message\"] directly to Gerrit; full findings remain separately present in the adapter result. Contract authority: ticket ACs and CONTRIBUTING.md:129-135 define a finding -1 as actionable input the author fixes before repushing. Caller sweep found only adapter._block/code_review_decision and voter posting the message; no caller depends on silent clipping. Test contract: in-process public adapter tier with only produce_code_review_verdict faked; preconditions assert 11 findings and over-cap text; postconditions require an explicit clip marker, an omitted-count note, and all 11 full translated findings preserved; short/exactly-at-cap controls must not claim truncation. Gate: focused pytest node, then repository gates. No new dependency or external behavior is introduced.","timestamp":1785249000906463001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"rebar-debug Phase 2 evidence: public adapter reproduction with 11 blocking findings longer than 240 characters showed the pre-fix mechanism at src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py:120-122: the message loop silently selected blocking[:10] and silently sliced normalized detail to 240 characters, while the header still claimed 11. This violates the actionable finding contract in CONTRIBUTING.md:129-135 and the ticket acceptance criteria. The final held-out oracle tests the public code_review_decision output at tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:223: with the fix absent it failed RED on the missing ellipsis; after the independent fix it passed GREEN; re-seeding the exact original raw slice/no-overflow branch returned it to RED; restoring the fix returned GREEN. Focused suite: 59 passed, 4 skipped. Original public-adapter scenario now renders 10 bounded bullets, an ellipsis on clipped detail, an exact one-finding overflow disclosure, and retains all 11 full machine-readable findings. Caller sweep found _summarize feeds only the adapter decision message and the voter posts it directly; no caller depends on silent clipping. Bounded sibling sweep of numeric slice caps in review_bot/llm found only hashes, normalization keys, or probes with explicit coverage bounds, not another actionable-feedback truncation. Fix restores truthful review output, adds no dependency, creates no new capability, and weakens no existing test. make check is green; default suite is running.","timestamp":1785250443323008001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final pre-push evidence: commit 59fab815d0a81184835c2b88475d9a8fbccde98f contains the adapter repair and public regression coverage, with DCO sign-off, Change-Id I00846da3467e1877ab0e45b5e55a60729210c6ff, and a verified rebar-ticket trailer. The final oracle covers 10/11/12 blocking findings, exact singular/plural omitted counts, exact 240-character clipped output with ellipsis, the exactly-240 no-truncation boundary, no overflow marker at the 10-finding cap, and preservation of full machine-readable details. It was RED with the fix absent and GREEN restored; defect mutations for raw clipping/no overflow, wrong plural, >=240 clipping, and omitted>=0 each returned the targeted RED. Gates: focused review-bot suite 62 passed, 4 skipped; make check passed; full default suite 7350 passed, 37 skipped, 114 deselected; final enabled model-backed review-code preview PASS with 0 blocking and 0 advisory. Awaiting explicit approval required by rebar-debug before pushing to Gerrit.","timestamp":1785252450957128001}],"created_at":1785219727674941001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b7184b76-c8f2-407f-b177-872c124402b3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"368a-a9df-da44-4444"},{"link_uuid":"de6081af-1224-4027-a1ae-3d182175fdaf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4090-6a28-428f-432d"},{"link_uuid":"53b8b558-6bbb-4a2f-a8c5-0dde22bac594","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fe2e-2cb7-3f27-4e64"},{"link_uuid":"2e37d2fa-6231-4968-b5d5-7201157104a3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1e2c-fff9-d1cf-463c"},{"link_uuid":"79a54098-275a-47e9-81c3-0da9e5c43736","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b266-6771-bb39-4bd6"},{"link_uuid":"e87bd537-c6b7-4718-bce6-fba880cba60d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a29d-7345-47f5-44b6"}],"description":"# Review-bot Gerrit comment truncates findings silently (no ellipsis, no \"N more\" note)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nFound incidentally while investigating ticket 368a (Gerrit line breaks — closed as not_a_bug). NOT the reported bug there; filed separately.\n\n`src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py:117-125` builds the blocking-finding comment the review bot posts on a Gerrit `-1`. Two silent truncations:\n\n1. `adapter.py:122` — `detail = str(f.get(\"finding\", \"\")).strip().replace(\"\\n\", \" \")[:240]`. A finding longer than 240 chars is clipped mid-sentence with NO ellipsis or marker, so the author cannot tell the text was cut. Verified by execution: a 690-char finding produced a 271-char line ending mid-token with no `…`.\n2. `adapter.py:120` — `for f in blocking[:10]`. With more than 10 blocking findings the rest are dropped with no \"N more\" note, so the comment understates how much must be fixed.\n\nThis matters because the comment is the actionable artifact for a blocked change: a truncated finding can be unactionable, and a hidden overflow reads as \"that's all of them\".\n\n## Why this is a defect\n\nThe codebase has its own convention for marking truncation: `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:440` emits an explicit `… n unchanged line(s) …` marker. The same module truncating without a marker is inconsistent with that established pattern. The rebar-debug protocol's own guidance is the general principle: a bounded output must not read as complete when it is not.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A finding clipped at the length cap ends with an explicit marker (e.g. ` …`) so the reader knows text was removed.\n- When more than the per-comment cap of blocking findings exist, the comment states how many were omitted (e.g. \"… and N more\").\n- The full detail remains discoverable (the cap stays — the point is disclosure, not raising the limit).\n- Existing review-bot comment tests keep passing; the marker is asserted by a new test.\n\n## Notes\n\nLow priority / UX. Confirmed by reading `adapter.py:117-125` and by executing the formatter with an over-length finding. Real posted bot comments observed in the wild are short (<=63 chars), so this triggers only on verbose blocking findings.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py","reason":"disclose per-finding clipping and blocking-finding overflow in the Gerrit summary"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot.py","reason":"RED/GREEN adapter regression covering both truncation boundaries and full-detail preservation"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1e2c-fff9-d1cf-463c"],["relates_to","4090-6a28-428f-432d"],["relates_to","a29d-7345-47f5-44b6"],["relates_to","b266-6771-bb39-4bd6"],["relates_to","fe2e-2cb7-3f27-4e64"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"548ba7b4-91eb-42c3-a165-36c8313956ad","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8f85-f170-1413-4040","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Review-bot Gerrit comment truncates findings with no ellipsis or overflow note","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2eca7ad0-22a9-4bea-a0b8-46cfe607648a","b7184b76-c8f2-407f-b177-872c124402b3","3f59740e-d82a-4999-91a5-2fc30e46b34b","548ba7b4-91eb-42c3-a165-36c8313956ad","f8e641c3-2a8f-4571-9168-18fd3aa5c840","c4b5f32f-1af7-4f1b-b215-573ba1d84700","60ae038c-d444-4add-9b82-d05446476dab","6b10931c-1e39-4781-8ab0-af0e86f84192","03420644-daf2-4ae5-9ec9-14a9410c3a3f","de6081af-1224-4027-a1ae-3d182175fdaf","53b8b558-6bbb-4a2f-a8c5-0dde22bac594","2e37d2fa-6231-4968-b5d5-7201157104a3","79a54098-275a-47e9-81c3-0da9e5c43736","bae0d851-715e-4111-a598-a5c06851ec17","e87bd537-c6b7-4718-bce6-fba880cba60d"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785254531535985269,"uuid":"9f9bba03-2ee6-4b86-afa0-e93aced68da4"}